//! `hg-os-types`: the frames of the broker's `OsPort` (OS integration
//! 6.1, OI-D1, OI-D26), generated by `hg-ipc-codegen` from
//! `idl/os.hgidl` and checked in (coding standard CS-ST-17). Layer L2,
//! tier R.
//!
//! An `OsPort` frame is the wire encoding of one message of
//! [`os::OsInput`] (from the OS) or [`os::OsCommand`] (to it): a 2-byte
//! ordinal naming the arm, then its fields. Each arm therefore has the
//! generated validator and Kani harness of any IPC message and fits the
//! 64 KiB message cap. `OsPort` is in-process, so these frames are
//! same-build only, like every `.hgidl` encoding (VER-1); recordings
//! carry the build ID.
//!
//! Do not edit `src/generated/`: change the `.hgidl` and run
//! `cargo run -p hg-ipc-codegen`. The `it` test fails if a file is stale.

/// The protocols, one module per `.hgidl` file.
pub mod generated {
    pub mod os;
}

pub use generated::os;

